# s5_up_split
#
# basis      s4_ars_charge peak 510,060 kB (T=16); s4 removed 763 MB of anon:[heap], named_frac_host
#            0.215 -> 0.614:
#              anon:[heap]                                             199.2 MB   0.381 of the peak
#              heap:comm.hpp:343:Dealer::recv_array<unsigned __int128>   91.3 MB   0.175   <- this step
#              heap:_Vector_base<unsigned __int128>::_M_allocate         67.1 MB   0.128
#              heap:vector<span<unsigned long>>::operator[]              56.6 MB   0.108
#              heap:Eigen::internal::handmade_aligned_malloc             49.6 MB   0.095
#            anon:[heap] not a target (unnamed); no skip declared.
# identity   matmul Beaver material, (ab + bc + ac) elements x 32 B (u128 share + u128 tag); FFN up:
#              (128*768 + 768*3072 + 128*3072) = 2,850,816 elements  x  32 B  =  91.2 MB
#            (measured 91.3 MB). QKV (128 x 768 x 2304): 69.2 MB.
# lever      column chunks (output column j depends on weight column j only); 4 chunks bound the
#            triple at 25.2 MB ((128*768 + 768*768 + 128*768) x 32 B; each chunk carries its own input
#            mask; the snapshot source's 22.8 MB omits one mask term). SHARK_UP_SPLITS default 4 =
#            3072/768 (target granularity).
# values     chunk weights copied from the filled layer weight (fill_span values kept); layer_input
#            and input-share stream unchanged; Beaver material differs (reconstructs to the same
#            value); ars charged in blocks of 98,304 = one chunk. Gate byte-identical.
# scope      GELU not moved into the chunk loop (would add 3 MB; one object per step).
# gap        retired campaign reached 386 MiB = 405 MB via malloc_trim(0) nine times per layer
#            (returns anon:[heap], not a target); belongs in off-path.md as an allocator trade.
# impl_snapshot: src/bert_instrumented_s5_up_split.cpp patches/s4_stream_and_charge.diff
# Library patch provenance (checked 2026-09-29 in shark-s5_up_split.sif on PALMA; earlier this line
# named patches/filebuf_read_buffer.diff alone, without s4's lrs.cpp charge-chunk change).
# /root/extra.diff in the image: md5 10d293d53bd828ca8e9a74350089686a = impl/patches/s4_stream_and_charge.diff
# (filebuf_read_buffer.diff, md5 7d5c715e..., plus lrs_charge_chunk.diff); s3 image: 7d5c715e....
# lrs.cpp contains LRS_CHARGE (3 matches; 0 in the s3 image); binary md5 34c250654146e06e1c9479c74dc00e41
# = binary_md5.txt of every published run of this step.
# s1 to s4 plus this step's lever.
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: shark::Dealer::recv_array<unsigned __int128>
# not_selectable_until: s4_ars_charge
# (re-measured 2026-09-29, freeze_mode=maxparty: s3_key_stream +5.1% at 1.1% spread, s4_ars_charge
# +14.4% at 3.0% spread, both paid. This free step follows them: its object is absent from s3's
# table and the largest attackable row of s4's, after s4 removed the 763 MB anon:[heap] key sub-arrays.)
OMP_NUM_THREADS=16
